\newlabel{fig:eval-multi}{{6}{9}{\textbf {Peak KV} on six models ($n{=}40$, $\mathrm {tp}{=}2$). Each panel is one family; groups are GSM8K and Game24. Bars are recompute, APC, \sys , and ForkServe+ (cream / tan / orange / purple). \sys {} and ForkServe+ share the spine. Annotated $\times $ is $M_{\mathrm {spine}}/M_{\mathrm {APC}}$: $0.72$--$0.75\times $ on GSM8K and $0.57$--$0.61\times $ on Game24, independent of checkpoint size, as \eqref {eq:mem} predicts}{figure.6}{}}
