\newlabel{fig:eval-radar}{{7}{10}{\textbf {Four systems on Qwen3-8B} ($n{=}80$, $\mathrm {tp}{=}2$, $D{=}512$). Each panel has its own axis. Quality is higher-better; peak KV and end-to-end time are the measured values, so a shorter bar is better. (a)~GSM8K. (b)~Game24. \Cref {fig:eval-radar} shows that \sys and ForkServe+ lower peak KV below APC on both workloads ($0.75\times $ on GSM8K, $0.62\times $ on Game24) while GSM8K quality stays with APC, and that ForkServe+ also lowers GSM8K end-to-end time from $36.0$\,s to $28.2$\,s}{figure.7}{}}
